 "intro": "Off the Aegates islands, west of Sicily, 241 BC, the last battle of the First Punic War. Rome’s new fleet of about 200 ships has been paid for by its richest citizens. You are the consul Gaius Lutatius Catulus.",
 "debrief": "In Polybius’s account, Catulus trained his crews through the summer. Carthage sent a relief fleet under Hanno, laden with supplies and short of marines, meaning to unload in Sicily and take on soldiers. Catulus waited at the Aegates and attacked at dawn although the wind was against him; the heavy Carthaginian ships were no match. Fifty were sunk and seventy taken. Carthage made peace, giving up Sicily and paying a large indemnity. The other choices are what-ifs.",
